    "avatarUrl": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIl82LkQ53ZNQJRcM-kUQY7Jo4Mf8FAmP-3bDqTaW98uOn7jcK2rg=s96-c",
    "profileCompleted": false,
    "subscriptionTier": "free",
    "profession": "CFO Danone Indonesia",
    "name": "Kerem Inan",
    "bio": "Kerem İnan is a senior finance executive with more than 20 years of international experience across emerging and developed markets, currently serving as Chief Financial Officer of Danone Indonesia, overseeing a ~$2B business.\n\nHe began his career at Danone in 2005 as a Management Trainee in Finance, holding multiple controlling and business planning roles within Danone Dairy Turkey. In 2010, he relocated to Paris to take on regional responsibilities as Regional Controller for Danone Waters EMEA, where he led financial integration and M&A projects.\n\nAfter returning to Turkey in 2013, Kerem joined Vodafone Turkey as Finance & Strategy Director, where he drove strategic planning, revenue optimization, and large-scale cost efficiency programs. In 2017, he rejoined Danone as CFO of Danone Turkey & Middle East, successfully leading a major profitability turnaround, including making the Hayat business profitable for the first time in 30 years of Danone’s history and delivering significant margin and cash improvements.\n\nIn 2021, Kerem moved to Asia as VP Finance & Strategy for Danone India & South Asia, overseeing financial strategy across India and Southeast Asia while executing major investment programs in India and Vietnam. Since 2023, he has served as CFO of Danone Indonesia, navigating a highly challenging macro and commercial environment while delivering record margin expansion, strong cash generation, balance sheet deleveraging, and structural value creation through disciplined P&L management.\n\nAcross his career, Kerem is recognized for combining deep financial rigor with business leadership, implementing long-term structural value creation frameworks (notably the 5X Value Creation model), driving cross-functional collaboration, and strengthening finance organizations as true business enablers. Despite severe topline pressures in recent years, his leadership has consistently delivered resilience, profitability, and cash discipline.\n\nKerem holds a degree in Industrial Engineering from Bilkent University (Full Scholarship) and has completed elite leadership programs including Danone’s LIONS Program and Vodafone’s Global Excellence Program. His long-term aspiration is to become a General Manager and, subsequently, pursue a global CFO role.\n\n\n",
